   "_note": "11-09 ACTION-SMOOTHNESS variant of rr_T1k_tc_s5.json (everything else identical, seed 5): caps coeff 0.1 = temporal smoothness of the policy MEAN as a PPO loss term (caps.py; CAPS, Mysore et al. 2021), plugged into rsl_rl's symmetry hook, logged as loss 'symmetry' (1 = a change of 0.01 normalised action on every actuator per control step; cap 25). Replaces rr_T1k_tcq_s5's reward-side action_rate / torque_rate terms, which also penalised PPO's exploration noise (zero residual + noise 0.1: -68 per step vs ~ +21 tracking) and collapsed the std (0.10 -> 0.03; training success 0.42 vs 0.88 for tc at 1e8 steps). Calibration (caps_calib.py, R3B final): L 13.5 (p50 12.3, p95 33.8), actor-gradient norm of L 21.9 vs PPO surrogate 13.7 -> coeff 0.1 mild (0.16 x surrogate), 0.5 strong (0.8 x).",
